A||||6||Bob Englert||What a way to end the year!||||1||
Z||000000||Bob Englert||12-31-2001||06:52 PM||||Last Thursday I was returning from a business trip in my 97 Legacy Brighton <BR>wagon when a lady made a left turn directly in front of my car while I was doing 45 mph (the speed limit), in the left lane of a 4 lane highway.  I had about 8-10ft. to process what was happening before I hit her car nearly head on.  I think the impact was at about 40 mph at about a 45 degree angle to her right front.  The driver said she didn't see me (I had lights on).<P>Both air bags deployed, the steering wheel was tilted to the left and the gear shift was pointing almost straight forward.  Except for the minor steering column deflection there was no intrusion into the passenger cabin at all.  The front of the car was completely crushed to the front wheels, and the hood folded.  All four doors worked after the impact, the driver door would hit the front left fender but still opened.  One interesting note was that the doors were locked before the impact, but apparently unlocked during the impact, since the emergency people were able to get to me quickly.<P>I saw the impact coming, and the next thing I saw was the deflated airbags smoking and me feeling like hell!  It was a hard hit.  After about 10 minutes I was able to get out of the car under my own power and I was taken to the local hospital with a bruised right knee from the lower dash and a very sore chest from the air bag.  I am very impressed and grateful on how well the car absorbed the impact and protected me from what could have been a very bad accident.  The other driver and passenger were a little more seriously hurt in their Pontiac GrandAM but will be OK.<P>One funny note, a VA state trooper was waiting to turn out from the road the lady was trying to turn into, so he saw the entire accident.  She will get a ticket and the trooper said I was not at fault at all.<P>The sad thing is the car had 128K and ran perfectly.  I had owned the car since it was new.  I had just had the timing belt replaced and major maintenance service done at the local dealer last month.  Subaru replaced the engine under warranty at about 56K and I had been using Mobil-1 for it's whole life.  I was really planning to keep the car for a long time, and will not get nearly what the car was worth to me or what it will cost to replace it.<P>Any advice on dealing with insurance adjusters would be appreciated.<P>While I am still very sore from the air bag, the car did a great job of protecting me from what could have been a very bad situation.  I will miss the car.  I wish Subaru had more competitive incentives available on their new Legacy models.<P>I have some pictures of the car but I don't know how to post them....<P>Happy New Year to all!<P>Bob Englert (still sore)<p>[This message has been edited by Bob Englert (edited 12-31-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jake_Dragon||12-31-2001||07:13 PM||||Sounds like it gave up the ghost to get you into the new year, glad to hear everyone is ok. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||flyntus||12-31-2001||08:36 PM||||Glad to hear you're okay & still with us!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||12-31-2001||11:42 PM||||I'm glad you survived the headon with just minor stiffness  Insurance adjustors will look at the 128K milage car, go to the Kelly Blue book and give you what the book says.  Not enough to get a decent replacement.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever3000||12-31-2001||11:53 PM||||Bob, sorry to hear that, but glad you're not seriously hurt.  Email pics to any of us and we'll get em on here.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||01-01-2002||12:11 AM||||Tell the adjuster about the recent work done. Provide receipts if you have them. Keep stressing what great shape the car was in. If their offer isn't to your liking, tell them you want more. When the wreck is 100% their customer's fault they don't have a very good position to argue from, don't let them bluff you.<P>PS: They are a LOT more worried about potential pain and suffering claims than property claims. If they're smart they won't piss you off over a few hundred when you are one attorney away from a few thousand in an easy out of court settlement. If you can't get what the car was worth to you one way, you can always get it the other.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Bob Englert||01-01-2002||12:23 AM||||Thanks all for the comments.<P>While I don't want to get a lawyer involved unless absolutely necessary, I will wait to see what the insurance company says.  4 days later and I still can't sleep on my side or get in the family car without difficulty.  It is getting easier but will take some time.  The air bag is for real!<P>Cheever, I will email you a couple of images tomorrow if you can post them.  I certainly hope that will be the end of my career as a crash dummy!<P>Again, happy new year to all!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
